==Spanish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|es|VL.|*iectāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|*iectō}}, from {{inh|es|LL.|iectāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|iectō}}, from {{inh|es|la|iactāre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|iactō}}. Doublet of the borrowing {{doublet|jactar|lang=es|notext=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{es-IPA}}

===Verb===
{{es-verb|ech|ar}}

# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[throw]], [[toss]], [[cast]] {{gloss|to release an object from one's grasp so that it moves through the air}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[pour]] {{gloss|to cause to flow in a stream from a container}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[put in]], [[add]]
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[let out]]
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[dump]]
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[emit]], [[give off]], [[send out]]
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[kick out]], [[expel]], [[throw out]] {{gloss|to forcibly remove}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to expel {{gloss|to remove from membership}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[fire]], [[dismiss]] {{gloss|to terminate employment}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[play]] {{gloss|to participate in a sport}}
#: {{ux|es|'''Echamos''' un partido.|inline=1|'''We're playing''' a match.}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[sprout]] {{gloss|to cause to grow from a seed}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[take]], [[have]] (a look at)
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[mail]], [[post]] {{gloss|to send through the mail/post}}
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[give]], [[bestow]] (a blessing); to [[put]] (a curse) on
# {{lb|es|transitive}} to [[turn]] (a key); to [[slide]] (a bolt)
